Subject: [PATCH v9 09/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Deliver posts to INBOX and
 sync it
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rqvvtqsnzoxqpqppunwpspvxrwplpvvk
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:05:06 +0000

Each post waits in a Dovecot INBOX that sits outside the maildir and
outside the sync, so it reaches neither Fastmail nor the readers of
lists until Pat moves it by hand. The account is the list's own and
nothing else arrives in it, so there is nothing to sort: new mail can
stay in INBOX on both sides.

Pat makes and names the account's folders on Fastmail. If lab-mail
named them too, every new folder would need a change to lab-mail
before it could reach anyone, so the hub carries every folder and
only a client names the ones it uses.

- INBOX is a folder of the maildir, so a post reaches Fastmail and
  every reader on the next sync.
- mbsync syncs every folder, and makes on Dovecot any folder made on
  Fastmail. Only its login may create a folder.
- The lists folder, which a Fastmail rule filled, goes away with the
  rule. The spec drops the rule and the moderation queue, and the jj
  maildir import lands in INBOX.
